                    Internal BBS menu prompt commands
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

LogicBBS is filled with internal menu prompt commands.
All commands can be replaced by external commands/doors, But the ACS flags
will be useless if you replace internal commands by external doors.
Some functions requires cosysop access or sysop access, or just an ACS flag
set. Several commands can have parameters after its name.




------------------------
BBS menu prompt commands
------------------------

A (Alter flagged files)
-----------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_DOWNLOAD

Files selected for download can be removed, or filenames can be added
to tag buffer, or user can clear buffer of selected files.



B (View bulletins)
------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_READ_BULLETINS

If you have created a bulletin area, user can view information here.
The menu file is called, bull0.txt or bull0.[acc].txt.
the bulletin files are called bull[number].txt or bull[number].[acc].txt.
If user writes B [number]. the bulletin number information will be shown
if found. If the user just writes B without number the menu will be shown.


C (Comment sysop)
-----------------
clearance Flags: ACS_COMMENTSYSOP

User can write a message directly to sysop with this command, User will
not be prompted for name or the private/public request.
If sysop selected forwarding of message to another area, message
will be saved in another conference.





D (Download menu)
-----------------
clearance Flags: ACS_DOWNLOAD, ACS_SYSOP_DOWNLOAD

Download selected files in current conference.
If the flag, ACS_SYSOP_DOWNLOAD, is enabled for user, it is possible
to download files directly from the harddrive, if full path and filename
is entered.


E (Enter message)
-----------------
clearance Flags: ACS_ENTER_MESSAGE, ACS_EALL_MESSAGES, ACS_ATTACH_FILE
                 ACS_DELETE_MESSAGE

Use "?" in message command prompt to view help.



F (File listings)
-----------------
clearance Flags: ACS_FILE_LISTINGS

List files in current conference. User can specify a dirlisting number.


G (Goodbye)
-----------

User logs off the node with this command.



H (Help)
--------

Not included yet.



J (Join conference)
-------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_JOIN_CONFERENCE

If command is entered without any name/number after, user will be shown
available conference accessable for this account/usertype.


L (Change Language/Texttype)
----------------------------

User can alter his texttype shown.. a list of available texttypes will be
shown to user.


M (Mode ansi or ascii)
----------------------

Select Ansi mode on/off...If Ansi is off, all ansi color sequences and
PC ansi sequence codes will be stripped.



N (Newfiles listings)
---------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_FILE_LISTINGS

List files since date. same as "F" but displays dirlisting from a specific
date.



O (Operator page)
-----------------
clearance Flags: ACS_PAGE_SYSOP, ACS_BREAKCHAT

User can page operator , and if he is available, sysop can enter chatmode
pressing function key [F1]. Sysop exits chatmode with [F1] or Ctrl-C.
User online time will be frezzed during chat.


Q (Quiet node)
--------------
clearance Flags: ACS_QUIET_NODE

User can tell the WHO door to hide what he is during while he is online.
If sysop selected a node quiet at startup, and user online deselect the
quiet node.
Node will automatically go back to quiet mode when user logs off the system.



R (Read message)
----------------
clearance Flags: ACS_READ_MESSAGE, ACS_SYSOP_READ

Entering messagebase in current conference. All available commands are
shown using "?" in the messagebase command prompt.

A normal user account will be able to read all mail addresssed from or
to him or messages addressed to ALL.
If the user is a co-sysop on the system, he will be able to read all
private messages written by users on the system, but messages that got
the co-sysop flag or sysop flag set, can only be seen by the co-sysop
himself or sysop.
If the ACS_SYSOP_READ flag is set, user will be able to read all mail
including mail addressed from/to sysop.

Special co/sysop function in messagebase are:

E - Edit header
F - Forward message to another user.
I - Ignore message. (Clear "received message" information)







S (User status)
---------------
clearance Flags: ACS_DISPLAY_USER_STATS

Displays current status of user.





T (Local system time)
---------------------

Shows current local time..



U (Upload menu)
---------------
clearance Flags: ACS_UPLOAD

Enter upload menu... User will be shown available space free for upload
and transfer protocol to use.



V (View file in dirlisting)
---------------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_VIEW_A_FILE, ACS_SYSOP_VIEW

User can view textfiles uploaded to current conference. If textfile contain
NON-ASCII characters, viewing will be aborted.

If user got the ACS_SYSOP_VIEW flag set, User can view files using
full path and filename.


W (Alter user information)
--------------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_EDIT_USER_NAME, ACS_EDIT_USER_LOCATION, 
                 ACS_EDIT_PHONE_NUMBER, ACS_EDIT_PASSWORD


User can alter the selected settings for newmailscan, screen length
and so on.



X (expert mode on/off)
----------------------

Select expertmode on/off.. If user selects expertmode, menu will not be
be displayed after each command execution.


Z (Zippy file search)
---------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_ZIPPY_TEXT_SEARCH

Search for a file in current conference. Search will search through
filenames, and not description.


1 (User account edit)
---------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_SYSOP_COMMANDS, ACS_ACCOUNT_EDITING

Enter user account editor.
All co-sysops got access to the internal user editor. but limitations
are made, to protect accounts.
A co-sysop cannot alter a users name, accesslevel, password or usertype.
A co-sysop cannot edit his own account from remote.




9 (Reserve node)
----------------
clearance Flags: ACS_SYSOP_COMMANDS

reserve current node for a user.


$ (Newmail scan ALL conferences)
--------------------------------

Rescan all mail conferences for new messages.



# (Freecredit account edit)
---------------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_SYSOP_COMMANDS

a co-sysop can enter the freecredit account maintance, and view or alter
accounts.



< (Jump 1 conference down)
--------------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_JOIN_CONFERENCE

Go one (relative) conference down.



> (Jump 1 conference up)
------------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_JOIN_CONFERENCE

Go one (relative) conference up.



? (Show conference menu)
------------------------

Display conference menu to user.



OLM (OnLine Message send to node)
---------------------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_OLM

Send a online message to a user on another node.




WHO (View users action on nodes)
--------------------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_WHO_IS_ONLINE

Display other node actions. User will be displayed username,location,
action for each node available.



J.file (Join conference - only fileareas shown)
-----------------------------------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_JOIN_CONFERENCE

Join a conference.. this command displays only filearea conferences available
to user.




J.msg (Join conference - only msgareas shown)
---------------------------------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_JOIN_CONFERENCE

Join a conference.. this command displays only message conferences available
to user.



Resetmsgbase (Message base setup)
--------------------------------
clearance Flags: ONLY WORKS FROM A LOCAL LOGIN

If sysop want to delete messages in message or minimize size of messagebase,
he can just enter this command.. Sysop will be prompted for lowest message to
keep.



OptimizeMsgbase (Message base setup)
------------------------------------
clearance Flags: ONLY WORKS FROM A LOCAL LOGIN

Sysop can reorganize messagebase structure to be much faster, if a lot of
messages if floating around and already deleted or old.
This command will go through messagebase and clean up. Messagebase will
be just as before and all unwanted mail will be gone.




MS (Locate Message)
-------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_READ_MESSAGE

Search for a message. If user cannot remember a number of a certain message
he can search for the message, using selected parameters asked when started.




RL (Relogin on node)
--------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_RELOGON

If user got access to this function he will be able to log off the node, 
and login once again, without disconnecting from the node.
A normal logoff and login procedure will be initiated.




DROPDTR (Remove user from node)
-------------------------------
clearance Flags: ACS_SYSOP_COMMANDS

Drop DTR (carrier) on another node






HYDRA (Hydra transfer indicator)
--------------------------------
clearance Flags: 

Start hydra transfer session.




RZ (Zmodem transfer indicator)
------------------------------
clearance Flags: 

Start a Zmodem transfer receive session.





CHAT (Multinode chat)
---------------------
clearance Flags: 
  
Enter multichat. User will be able to "talk" to users on other nodes.
functions available can be viewed when multichat is entered.

